Subject: [PATCH] nvenc: do not force an IDR on a bitrate-only reconfigure (meshharbor FR-62 A2)

A maxrate-only reconfigure of a cq-VBR NVENC stream (our config: averageBitRate
stays 0, only maxBitRate/vbvBufferSize move) applies live and needs no IDR.
Upstream sets resetEncoder=forceIDR=1 on any rate change; on a slow relay that
keyframe is multiple seconds of transit on every AIMD step (FR-62 A0 measured a
rate-caused IDR on 20/20 rungs, apply ~0.005 ms). Applying the new encodeConfig
without a reset is exactly OBS's dynamic-bitrate path.

Carried in meshharbor's vendored FFmpeg only; would upstream behind a private
reconfig_idr option (default 1).
---
--- a/libavcodec/nvenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/nvenc.c
@@ -2850,9 +2850,12 @@
         }
 
         if (reconfig_bitrate) {
-            params.resetEncoder = 1;
-            params.forceIDR = 1;
-
+            // meshharbor fork (FR-62 A2): a bitrate-only reconfigure (our NVENC
+            // keeps averageBitRate == 0 and moves only maxBitRate/vbv for a
+            // cq-VBR stream) applies LIVE and needs no IDR. Upstream forces one
+            // (resetEncoder = forceIDR = 1); on a slow relay that keyframe is
+            // multiple seconds of transit on every AIMD step. Applying the new
+            // encodeConfig without a reset is exactly OBS's dynamic-bitrate path.
             needs_encode_config = 1;
             needs_reconfig = 1;
         }
